PURPOSE: prove the portable template's #ifdef discipline is what makes the kernels
compile under hipcc. Inject an UNGUARDED CUDA-only construct into a SCRATCH copy
of a kernel and show hipcc errors. (Scratch only — the committed tree stays clean;
the scratch dir /tmp/pk_hip_neg is deleted after capture.)

Two demonstrations:
  (A) a bare, unguarded cudaMemcpyAsync (CUDA runtime API; absent under HIP);
  (B) the REAL Todo 19 bug reproduced: an unguarded 32-bit warp-shuffle mask
      (the pre-fix PK_FULL_MASK), which HIP rejects (mask must be 64-bit).

==============================================================================
(A) SCRATCH COPY of gelu.cu with an injected UNGUARDED cudaMemcpyAsync
==============================================================================
Injected host function (NO #ifndef POLYKERNEL_HIP guard):
    void injected_portability_bug(const pk_bf16 *src, pk_bf16 *dst) {
      cudaMemcpyAsync(dst, src, 256, cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice, 0);
    }

COMMAND:
  hipcc --offload-arch=gfx1101 -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP -Ikernels/template \
        -c /tmp/pk_hip_neg/gelu_neg.cu -o /tmp/pk_hip_neg/gelu_neg.o
  exit code: 1 (FAILED, as required)

HIPCC ERROR OUTPUT:
