     71 |   cudaMemcpyAsync(dst, src, 256, cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice, 0);
  /tmp/pk_hip_neg/gelu_neg.cu:71:3: error: use of undeclared identifier 'cudaMemcpyAsync'; did you mean 'hipMemcpyAsync'?
     71 |   cudaMemcpyAsync(dst, src, 256, cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice, 0);
     71 |   cudaMemcpyAsync(dst, src, 256, cudaMemcpyDeviceToDevice, 0);
  1 warning and 2 errors generated when compiling for gfx1101.

==============================================================================
(B) REAL BUG REPRO: unguarded 32-bit warp-shuffle mask (pre-fix PK_FULL_MASK)
==============================================================================
Scratch kernel calls __shfl_xor_sync with an UNGUARDED 32-bit mask 0xffffffffu
(exactly what kernel_common.h's PK_FULL_MASK was before the Todo 19 fix):
    PK_DEVICE_INLINE float repro_unguarded_32bit_mask(float v) {
      return __shfl_xor_sync(0xffffffffu, v, 1); // 32-bit mask
    }

COMMAND:
  hipcc --offload-arch=gfx1101 -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP -Ikernels/template \
        -c /tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.cu -o /tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.o
  exit code: 1 (FAILED, as required)

HIPCC ERROR OUTPUT:
  In file included from /tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.cu:1:
  In file included from kernels/template/kernel_common.h:52:
  /nix/store/jc7q7dm8y1r2317sg888mi7pxzarg7m2-clr-7.2.3/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_warp_sync_functions.h:307:62: error: static assertion failed due to requirement 'sizeof(unsigned int) == 8': The mask must be a 64-bit integer. Implicitly promoting a smaller integer is almost always an error.
  /tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.cu:6:10: note: in instantiation of function template specialization '__shfl_xor_sync<unsigned int, float>' requested here
      6 |   return __shfl_xor_sync(0xffffffffu, v, 1); // UNGUARDED 32-bit mask -> HIP error
  failed to execute:/nix/store/pr6n8zlqczbgsgzjrr1an1zzlp0hd7g7-hipClang/bin/clang++  --offload-arch=gfx1101 -O3  -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP -Ikernels/template -c -x hip /tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.cu -o "/tmp/pk_hip_neg/mask_neg.o"

==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
Both unguarded constructs make hipcc FAIL (exit 1):
  (A) cudaMemcpyAsync is undeclared under -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP (hipcc even suggests
      hipMemcpyAsync) -> a CUDA-only API call cannot appear unguarded.
  (B) a 32-bit shuffle mask trips HIP's static_assert(sizeof(mask)==8) -> the
      genuine bug that the Todo 19 PK_FULL_MASK guard fixes.
This proves the #ifdef discipline (every backend-specific construct behind a
guard in kernel_common.h) is ENFORCED by hipcc: remove the discipline and the
compile breaks. With the discipline in place, all 7 kernels compile clean
(see reports/w4_hipcc_compile.log).

Scratch dir /tmp/pk_hip_neg deleted after capture; committed tree unchanged.
